From: Mohithash <shahjespuri@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 8 Sep 2026 16:01:37 +0000
Subject: WebView: clear the Vulkan provider pointer before releasing
 it

RenderThreadManager keeps the raw pointer InitVk gave it for as long as
the functor lives, but OnContextDestroyed releases the provider first
and the functor is destroyed later, so the pointer dangles in between.
Nothing reads it in that window, which is why it went unnoticed; with
the dangling raw_ptr detector on it kills the host app every time a
page's renderer is replaced under a Vulkan HWUI. Hand the manager a
null pointer before the provider goes away.

License: GPL-2.0-or-later - https://spdx.org/licenses/GPL-2.0-or-later.html
---
 android_webview/browser/gfx/aw_draw_fn_impl.cc | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

diff --git a/android_webview/browser/gfx/aw_draw_fn_impl.cc b/android_webview/browser/gfx/aw_draw_fn_impl.cc
index c4a8c64ff1..8b6803cf9c 100644
--- a/android_webview/browser/gfx/aw_draw_fn_impl.cc
+++ b/android_webview/browser/gfx/aw_draw_fn_impl.cc
@@ -269,6 +269,12 @@ void AwDrawFnImpl::OnContextDestroyed() {
   }
 
   scoped_secondary_cb_draw_.reset();
+  // InitVk handed the render thread manager a non-owning pointer to the
+  // provider; take it back before the provider is released, or it dangles
+  // until the functor is destroyed.
+  if (vulkan_context_provider_) {
+    render_thread_manager_.SetVulkanContextProviderOnRT(nullptr);
+  }
   vulkan_context_provider_.reset();
 }
 
